{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTraceCyclicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTraceCyclicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Hom"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.gram_symm_of_rep_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.gram_symm_of_rep_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L208-L221","doc":"**Bridge brick.** If `τ = ∑_λ w_λ · trace ∘ ρ_λ` with each `ρ_λ` multiplicative\non the bilinear product `B` (`ρ_λ (B u v) = ρ_λ u * ρ_λ v`), then the Gram matrix\n`G_{i,j} = τ (B (e i) (e j))` is symmetric. Combined with `cyclic_of_gram_symm`,\nthis gives full cyclicity with no per-pair `Fin`-computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.isCyclic_weighted_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.isCyclic_weighted_sum","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L180-L188","doc":"**Brick — a finite weighted sum of cyclic functionals is cyclic.** This is\nthe shape of `tr_M = ∑_λ w_λ · χ_λ`: given each `χ_λ` cyclic (the previous\nbricks), the Markov trace is cyclic, hence Gram-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.smul","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L174-L177","doc":"**Brick — cyclic functionals are closed under a scalar multiple.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.add","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L168-L171","doc":"**Brick — cyclic functionals are closed under `+`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.isCyclic_trace_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.isCyclic_trace_comp","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L159-L165","doc":"**Brick — characters are cyclic.** The trace of any matrix representation\n`ρ : A →ₐ[R] Matrix n n R` is a cyclic functional (`Matrix.trace_mul_comm`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.IsCyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.IsCyclic","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L156-L157","doc":"A functional `τ : A → R` is **cyclic** (a trace) if `τ (x·y) = τ (y·x)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.cyclic_of_gram_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.cyclic_of_gram_symm","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L120-L138","doc":"**Cyclicity from Gram symmetry** — the `whnf`-free reduction, over any\n`Fintype` index. Given the finite Gram matrix `G_{i,j} = τ (B (e i) (e j))` is\nsymmetric, `τ (B u v) = τ (B v u)` for all `u, v`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_B_gram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_B_gram","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L103-L118","doc":"**Gram form.** `τ (B u v) = ∑_{i,j} u_i v_j · G_{i,j}` with `G_{i,j} = τ (B (e i) (e j))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_B_right_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_B_right_expand","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L90-L101","doc":"Expand `τ (B w v)` over the right basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_B_left_expand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_B_left_expand","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L76-L88","doc":"Expand `τ (B u v)` over the left basis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.tau_sum","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L66-L74","doc":"`τ` commutes with finite sums (additivity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.B_sum_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.B_sum_right","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L55-L63","doc":"`B u ·` commutes with finite sums in the right argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.B_sum_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.B_sum_left","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L46-L52","doc":"`B · v` commutes with finite sums in the left argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.basis_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.basis_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L35-L39","doc":"Basis decomposition `u = ∑ᵢ uᵢ • eᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.BilinearTrace.e","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/BilinearTraceCyclicity.lean#L32-L33","doc":"Standard basis vector `e i = Pi.single i 1` on `ι → R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}